In September I decided I was going to play a dungeon level a day, every day 
until the character ascended or died sufficiently deep enough in the 
dungeons (Medusa, Castle, etc). My lawful human female priest died quickly 
thanks to an owlbear and two tame large cats who couldn't be troubled to 
help the one who gave them delicious tripe rations.

On October 1st I started a new game with an orcish barbarian. One thing 
that I've found to be common between both games is that NetHack is pretty 
boring. This is the first time I've kept logs of a NetHack game and most 
levels are just "Found a wand of lightning" and "Stupid werejackals".

The most interesting part so far has been the orcish barbarian's arrival at 
Mine's End, acquiring a hoard of gems and the guaranteed luckstone.

I am playing other games of NetHack but the orcish barbarian game is being 
played very slowly and so far it doesn't seem to be that dangerous. 
Realistically I chalk this up to the robust orc and barbarian combination 
rather than exercising patience.


